## Summary

SmartEditTool — a new tool wrapper in src/tool_wrappers.rs that intercepts edit_file "not found" failures and augments them with precise location context.

### What it does
When edit_file fails because old_text wasn't found, instead of just saying "not found", the agent now sees:
• **📍 Nearest match at line N** — the exact line number where the closest match lives
• **5-line snippet** — the actual file content at that location so the agent can see what's really there
• ⚠️ Whitespace hint — if the text matches perfectly except for indentation, it says so explicitly

### How it works
• find_nearest_match() takes the first non-empty line of `old_text`, normalizes whitespace, and searches the file for matching lines
• When multiple matches exist, it picks the one with the most consecutive matching lines
• Whitespace-only diff detection compares trimmed vs exact content across all old_text lines
• Files >100KB are skipped (graceful fallback to original error)
• Missing/unreadable files produce no augmentation, no panic

### Wiring
In build_tools(): `with_auto_check(edit_tool) → with_smart_edit(...) → with_truncation(...) → with_recovery_hints(...)`. SmartEditTool fires first (positional context), then RecoveryHintTool adds escalating strategy ("use read_file", "try write_file instead").

### Tests
11 new tests: 6 unit tests for find_nearest_match (exact match, whitespace-only diff, no match, empty input, all-whitespace, snippet length limit) and 5 async integration tests for the full wrapper (passthrough success, passthrough non-not-found errors, line number augmentation, whitespace detection, missing file handling).
